  "commentary": "Centralized is the pooled-data upper bound. FL Baseline uses 3 clients, 15 communication rounds, one local epoch, and FedAvg. FL+DNA only adds DNA encode/decode for local model updates. FL+DP only adds client-update clipping and Gaussian noise. FL+DNA+DP applies DP first, then DNA transports the DP-protected update. Secure Aggregation uses pairwise masks so the server only observes the aggregate update, not individual client updates. DNA Transform Defense makes DNA the core update transformation via sequence-seeded block mixing and selective attenuation."
